  "raw_text": "Step 1: To find the remainder when the $100^{\\text{th}}$ term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4, we can first observe the pattern of remainders when dividing the Fibonacci numbers by 4.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the first few terms of the Fibonacci sequence modulo 4 to identify any repeating patterns:\n- $F_1 = 1 \\mod 4 = 1$\n- $F_2 = 1 \\mod 4 = 1$\n- $F_3 = F_1 + F_2 = 1 + 1 = 2 \\mod 4 = 2$\n- $F_4 = F_2 + F_3 = 1 + 2 = 3 \\mod 4 = 3$\n- $F_5 = F_3 + F_4 = 2 + 3 = 5 \\mod 4 = 1$\n- $F_6 = F_4 + F_5 = 3 + 1 = 4 \\mod 4 = 0$\n- $F_7 = F_5 + F_6 = 1 + 0 = 1 \\mod 4 = 1$\n- $F_8 = F_6 + F_7 = 0 + 1 = 1 \\mod 4 = 1$\n\nStep 3: Notice that the sequence of remainders starts repeating every 6 terms: 1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 0.\n\nStep 4: Since the sequence repeats every 6 terms, we can determine the remainder of the $100^{\\text{th}}$ term by finding the position of 100 within the repeating cycle. We do this by calculating $100 \\mod 6$.\n\nStep 5: Calculate $100 \\mod 6 = 4$. This means the $100^{\\text{th}}$ term corresponds to the 4th term in the repeating sequence (1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 0).\n\nStep 6: The 4th term in the repeating sequence is 3.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{3}<|im_end|>",
